.TH MTPD 8
.SH NAME
mtpd \- files to a PC over MTP (Media Transfer Protocol)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBmtpd\fR [\fB\-r\fR \fIroot\fR] [\fB\-l\fR \fIline\fR]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Mtpd
offers the folder
.I root
(default
.BR /home/flipper ,
the same tree as
.BR /ext )
to a computer as one MTP storage, so that Windows and Linux copy files
to and from the Flipper with their own drivers (Galtzagorriak MINIX, spec
R10.4).
.B /home
stays mounted: MTP works file by file, through the file system.
.PP
On the Flipper,
.B devd
starts
.B mtpd
when the computer configures the USB device and it ends on detach (the
USB side is planned, T29b).
Without
.BR \-l ,
it speaks on standard input and output; with
.B \-l
on
.I line
(in QEMU,
.BR /dev/mtpline ,
the second serial line).
It ends when the computer goes, with status 0.
.TP
.B \-r \fIroot\fR
the storage's folder.
.TP
.B \-l \fIline\fR
the device to speak on.
.SH "WHAT THE COMPUTER SEES"
Folders and plain files under
.I root
only: no device files, FIFOs, or anything on another file system.
An object handle is the file's inode number, so it stays valid while the
file is renamed on the Flipper.
Started as root,
.B mtpd
runs as the owner of
.I root
(user
.BR flipper ),
never as root; it refuses to run when root owns
.IR root .
New files get that user's
.BR umask .
.PP
A name longer than the file system takes (14 characters on MINIX V2, 60
on V3), or with
.BR / ,
a control character,
.B .
or
.BR .. ,
is refused with an error, never cut.
A file the computer was sending when it cancelled or the cable came out
is removed.
Files are at most 4 GiB \- 1 byte.
Dates are UTC.
.SH OPERATIONS
GetDeviceInfo, OpenSession, CloseSession, GetStorageIDs, GetStorageInfo,
GetNumObjects, GetObjectHandles, GetObjectInfo, GetObject,
GetPartialObject, SendObjectInfo, SendObject, DeleteObject (a folder with
everything in it), MoveObject, GetObjectPropsSupported, GetObjectPropDesc,
GetObjectPropValue, SetObjectPropValue (the file name: rename),
GetObjectPropList (depth 0), GetDevicePropDesc and GetDevicePropValue
(the friendly name).
Anything else gets Operation_Not_Supported.
Events: ObjectAdded and ObjectRemoved for changes made over MTP,
StorageInfoChanged (at most one per 2 s) and StoreAdded.
.SH "THE STREAM"
Without USB, MTP's three paths travel in frames on one byte stream, each
a 2-byte little-endian header and its bytes.
From the computer: 1 to 1024, that many bytes of bulk OUT; 0xFFFF, cancel
(USB's Cancel request); 0, hang up (the cable pulled).
From
.BR mtpd :
1 to 1024, bulk IN; 0x8000 plus the length, an event (USB's interrupt IN).
The containers inside are exactly USB's.
.B tools/mtphost.py
speaks it.
.SH MEMORY
About 7.4 KB while it runs (the 1 KB data buffer, the 2 KB parent ring,
paths, one directory buffer; no heap), 0 when it does not.
.SH FILES
.TP 20
.B /home/flipper
the storage.
.TP
.B /dev/mtpline
QEMU only: the test line.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR jiggle (1).
.br
The manual's chapter "Files to a PC over USB" (docs/manual/usb-files.md).
.SH BUGS
Until the free-space counters of spec O.5 exist, the free space is
reported as unknown.
The desktop PIN lock does not exist yet; when it does, the storage is
hidden while it is on.
